 "observations": [
  "col_left L1, L17, col_right L22, L30, L40: the d of «introductorius», «Lidzbarski», «longitudinis», «(adn.» (R30) and «medium» is printed broken, its bowl open, like rl; read d.",
  "col_left L3, L7, L18, L23, L27, L31, L32, L34, L40, L44, col_right L14, L17, L41: many t's are printed with the left part of their crossbar faint or missing, so that they look like l («octavae», «planetis», «Liechtenstein», «Almagesti», «planetarum», «terminus», «stilum», «litterae», «alphabeti», «sumptae», «Loftus», «longitudo», «respectu», «variatio», «semidiametrus», «motus»); read t.",
  "col_left L6, col_right L29: the m of «triplicitatum» and of «emendandae» is printed broken, like ı and n; the first n of «emendandae» is printed like ıı.",
  "col_left L7: a thin slanting stroke (1.7 by 2.3 points) under the n of «ascendente», 2.1-4.4 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L10: the 7 of «297» is printed 9.2 points tall, its stem drawn 1.7 points below the baseline and ending in a foot turned to the left, like an old-style 7; the other 7s of the page stand on the baseline (7.6 points tall). Read 7: Part I p. 297 n. 5 names Libri.",
  "col_left L23: a speck (1.1 by 0.7 points) under the s of «terminus», 0.8-1.5 points below the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_left L24: the middle figure of «200» is printed broken: only its left stroke and two small pieces of its right side are printed. Its ink lies within the outline of the 0 of this type (and of the 6); read 0: the place cited, Part I p. 200, explains the expression « linea x ». «*x*» is an italic x.",
  "col_left L25: the h and the o of «horariae» are printed broken (the h like li, the o open); read h and o.",
  "col_left L26: «296; cfr. horae» ends without a point, as printed.",
  "col_left L29: the L of «{sc:lxxviii}» is printed blotted, its stem and foot filled in; read L.",
  "col_left L33: «=» is printed as a long equals sign. The s of «stellae» is printed broken, its lower terminal apart like a point (1.7 by 1.9 points); it is not a point.",
  "col_left L39, L42, L43, col_right L12: the o of «longitudines» (L39) is printed open at the top, the last o of «meridiano», of «quomodo» and the o of «modis» in two strokes, like ( ); read o.",
  "col_left L43: the figures of «*20*» after «deducta» are printed broken: of the 2 the upper curve and the foot remain, of the 0 the top and the right side. Their ink lies within the outline of the italic 2 and 0 of «*19-20*» in the same line (98 and 99.8 per cent of it, against 84-91 per cent for the upright 0, 7 and 9 of the page); read *20*: the place cited, Part I p. 20 (lines 1-4), tells how longitudes were derived from the times of eclipses. The a of «deducta» is printed broken, its bowl reduced to a point.",
  "col_left L46: a round speck (1.3 by 1.6 points) in the indentation before «(adn.», 4.1-5.7 points above the baseline, and a smaller one (0.6 by 0.8 point) after the final point are not transcribed.",
  "col_right L2: «{sc:lxxvii}-{sc:viii}» is printed so, the second numeral abbreviated. The n after «{sc:xviii}» is printed broken, like ı and ).",
  "col_right L4: «λόξωσις» is Greek, read at 4,800 dpi: the acute is cast joined to the top of the ο and rises from it like the stem of a δ, as in βασιλικός (p. 380); the δ of this type has a hooked head (ἴδιον, p. 391). The b of «obliquatio» is printed broken, like l and ).",
  "col_right L9: «al-Battānī» has bars over the second a and the last i, measured with macron_audit.py.",
  "col_right L12: a thin stroke (1.0 by 2.3 points) between «parens» and «in», 0.2-2.5 points below the baseline, is not transcribed; it has no head and is not a comma.",
  "col_right L18: the hyphen of «ex-» is printed as a short point at mid height (1.6 by 1.0 points).",
  "col_right L21: the foot of the descender of the q of «quid» is printed apart from the letter, 1.7-2.5 points below the baseline; it is not a sign under the u.",
  "col_right L25: a speck (1.4 by 1.8 points) in the indentation before «rall.», on the baseline, is not transcribed.",
  "col_right L36: the s of «nonagesimo» is printed broken, its lower terminal apart like a point (1.4 by 1.9 points); it is not a point.",
  "col_right L37: the a and the n of the last «(adn.» are printed broken; read a and n.",
  "col_right L43: a round speck (1.2 by 1.1 points) under the e of «correctio», 2.0-3.1 points below the baseline, is not transcribed; it is not a dot below."
 ],
